ck over the primary repository''s version tags, commit\nmessages naming the component descriptor''s digest. fabric-platform-git reads\nand writes components.yaml schema 2 and 3, refuses described under schema 2\nby name, and plan::apply is now an exhaustive match. The console gives each\ndiagnostic its own wording, invalid with its reason.\n\nAn evaluator example, the one the release will run, reads\nghcr.io/fieldstatenz/saas-fabric 0.3.0-preview.15 today and answers\nundescribed, as it should.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Registries become integrations an operator registers, read only at public addresses and with a credential only where it was registered\n\nSlice 3 of ADR 0026.\n\nfabric-registry builds a registry from settings: an HTTPS endpoint, the host\nit names repositories by, a realm rule for its kind (GHCR''s and Docker Hub''s\nrealms are fixed; a distribution registry''s is recorded when it is\nregistered; the deployment''s own follows its first challenge and then holds\nit), an optional credential presented only for the repositories registered\nunder it, and an address policy. Authentication follows WWW-Authenticate,\nsends a credential only to a realm the kind allows and never across origins,\nand a realm refusing it marks it refused so a sweep does not retry it into a\nlocked account. An operator''s registry is read only at public addresses,\nchecked after resolution on every connection and before any IP-literal hop.\nRegistries routes the Registry port by host and never falls through.\n\nThe control plane gains registries as integration state beside the Git\napplications'': records in the instance partition, credentials in the secret\nstore under a server-minted id, proven before recorded, audited, with their\nown errors and routes under /api/integrations/registries. The same router\nserves Platform Management. The console''s Integrations page gains an Image\nregistries section that shows what was proven, never \"connected\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* The catalogue selects a described component and the server resolves it; what it declares is in effect beside what the operator authored\n\nSlice 4 of ADR 0026.\n\nThe catalogue gains a described component kind carrying a resolution: the\nrepository, version, primary and component-descriptor digests, the commit,\nwhen it was resolved, and a frozen copy of the whole component descriptor,\nvalidated on every read with its own version''s rules. A catalogue is written\nat the lowest apiVersion that expresses it, v1 byte-identical until a\ndescribed component exists and v2 after, so an older build refuses it by\nnaming the version. The fields and resources a component descriptor declares\nare in effect beside authored ones through one accessor every reader uses:\nvalidation, the publish-time cross-application check on both sides, the\nruntime catalogue and a client''s configuration.\n\nSaving a draft takes a request shape of its own that cannot carry a\nresolution, a digest or declared content, and refuses a change of kind.\nSelecting a version is a command of its own that the control plane resolves\nthrough the release-unit rule, within a budget that also bounds the registry\nstore read, before the pure write, with its own refusals and audit.\n\nThe console gains the picker, read-only declared views labelled with the\ncomponent descriptor''s digest and resolution time, the effective fields in a\nclient''s configuration, and — deferred here from slice 3 — which registry\neach managed component is read through, anonymously or with its credential.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: trigger existing security scans after targeting main\n\n* Reject credentials in blob redirects and test bounded registry reads\n\n* Apply pinned rustfmt layout to redirect fixture\n\n* Keep redirect redaction-test diagnostics free of secret values\n\n* State registry refusal and credential activation guarantees precisely\n\n* Count actual HTTP listing requests under challenge-based authentication\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: IngeniousRiley <336672273+IngeniousRiley@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYQuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi/8QAGq4CV7J4obILmTaB6UQktnz\nWKXmqXkn8SaQ+p/R9nPxIctmU5wpG6l6OeTfuB/FjoEjZZbI8GSDr1CyHL/zb3xo\ng4QDjlxeWtCoiBIPm++vXH++kWCYtcz60idEb3OdALd81r4C7MQx8svSr/nwuJlG\n5BccwOxZ7vUbUp/eP9l0yNyH9eYsqXu7yHpzCxppu+z7Ba7lrCymXw2IdCKoURF6\nR02ipDMQWTNiMMmoTK5tC059qNBO8DA6KnkEpH4EI6Dp3eQjU0C93vUhzIBPxOj4\n4HYDiBJhbA33syCGqC99B7DZejOdt8wyu1ryk5iewb9xYz+yypqkQEU7xWZy8wFe\n356+k3dUV3qtEFk2oL22+GWmaRpgm1b5HIeq4ntl9/r91wt6Efwva5Dgf1x8DJ2T\nPxIOizh6cX55N1+/8l2m3E74o+++hpag3kRCTWv/C094VKW9bkAd4ZjsOOeMkr+m\nTGliCVQ2dQK8a08zxu3OQvwoNyY5B0KXAe/0P5xLthBZD45g+9id+CmalguoDYPC\nioJs5oG58b6rBcGxpmCIAWWtEbF331I3x+0OgfUFJ8rCXhnIXWhT4Baf7bQfKgDq\nQgkZf5GIIo7J8V5d1q6TYRdm7wToeXis3YcenP1H/AQymiu1NOM/bDfbAjGvBYFk\nA33ApMa0lxQTGSZauiHt\n=4tJi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T22:39:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/15a73231939349d870320e29c0b6a799b83afbab","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDE1YTczMjMxOTM5MzQ5ZDg3MDMyMGUyOWMwYjZhNzk5YjgzYWZiYWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/d28fc97d76f0319fb188b2d490149098e3db0a55","sha":"d28fc97d76f0319fb188b2d490149098e3db0a55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/d28fc97d76f0319fb188b2d490149098e3db0a55"}],"sha":"15a73231939349d870320e29c0b6a799b83afbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/15a73231939349d870320e29c0b6a799b83afbab"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/d28fc97d76f0319fb188b2d490149098e3db0a55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:20:13Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T22:20:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Registries become integrations an operator registers, read only at public addresses and with a credential only where it was registered (#97)\n\n* ADR 0026: a component describes itself in an artifact attached to its image, and the catalogue selects it from registries an operator registers\n\nA component publishes a component descriptor, a small JSON document naming\nits images by role and digest, the capabilities it needs, the configuration\nfields a client supplies and the Data API resources it exposes. It is an OCI\nartifact attached to the component''s primary image and pushed last, so the\nimage a person selects carries the description of the software.\n\nOne rule, written once, decides whether a version is a release unit, and both\nPlatform Management''s discovery and the catalogue''s selection apply it.\nRegistries become operator-registered integrations: closed kinds, public\naddresses only, and credentials presented only to the repositories they were\nregistered for. The catalogue gains a described component kind that the\nserver resolves, and the save request can no longer carry what the server\nresolved. Fabric''s own release attaches its component descriptor, and the\nattach step lands only after every reader.\n\nPointer paragraphs record what this amends in ADRs 0008, 0021, 0023 and 0024.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Describe a component in one contract crate, and move the shapes it shares with the catalogue into it\n\nSlice 1 of ADR 0026. fabric-component, in neither plane and with no\ntransport, owns the component descriptor: its versioned envelope, a strict\nJSON reader that refuses duplicate keys and oversized documents before\nparsing, the repository, digest, role, name and version rules, a\ncanonical renderer from the authored component.yaml, and the\nPlatformCapability type. The configuration-field and application-resource\nshapes and their validators move into it from fabric-client-model, which\nre-exports them at their old paths; fixtures prove a catalogue and a client\ndocument re-render byte-identically, and every validator message is\nunchanged.\n\ncomponent.yaml describes saas-fabric by the three roles the platform already\npins. The release matrix gains each image''s role and marks runtime primary,\ninert until the attach job; a pull-request test renders component.yaml and\nchecks it against that matrix. Nothing is published.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Read a component through the descriptor attached to its image, by one rule, with every digest computed\n\nSlice 2 of ADR 0026: the readers. Nothing attaches a descriptor yet.\n\nThe registry adapter now computes every digest it records: a tag is resolved\nby HEAD and then read by digest and hashed, a Docker-Content-Digest that\ndisagrees with the body is refused, and a bounded cache holds only bytes\nalready verified against their digest. Every body is bounded before it is\nparsed, a pagination link off the origin is refused rather than ending the\nlist, redirects stay on the origin except for blobs, and a blob''s redirects\nare followed by hand so the pull token reaches the registry''s own origin and\nnever a CDN hop, on chains of any length. Revisions are read from config\nlabels and manifest annotations. component_descriptor reads referrers through\nthe API and the tag-schema fallback, merged, checks every candidate manifest\nby digest, and returns the one document, or why there is not one.\n\nfabric-platform-management gains the release-unit rule, written once:\nevaluate() answers complete, undescribed, incoherent or invalid with a closed\nreason, in ADR 0026 section 3''s order. Platform Management reads a described\ncomponent through it: ArtifactSource::Described and Release::Described,\ndiscovery and rollback over the primary repository''s version tags, commit\nmessages naming the component descriptor''s digest. fabric-platform-git reads\nand writes components.yaml schema 2 and 3, refuses described under schema 2\nby name, and plan::apply is now an exhaustive match. The console gives each\ndiagnostic its own wording, invalid with its reason.\n\nAn evaluator example, the one the release will run, reads\nghcr.io/fieldstatenz/saas-fabric 0.3.0-preview.15 today and answers\nundescribed, as it should.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Registries become integrations an operator registers, read only at public addresses and with a credential only where it was registered\n\nSlice 3 of ADR 0026.\n\nfabric-registry builds a registry from settings: an HTTPS endpoint, the host\nit names repositories by, a realm rule for its kind (GHCR''s and Docker Hub''s\nrealms are fixed; a distribution registry''s is recorded when it is\nregistered; the deployment''s own follows its first challenge and then holds\nit), an optional credential presented only for the repositories registered\nunder it, and an address policy. Authentication follows WWW-Authenticate,\nsends a credential only to a realm the kind allows and never across origins,\nand a realm refusing it marks it refused so a sweep does not retry it into a\nlocked account. An operator''s registry is read only at public addresses,\nchecked after resolution on every connection and before any IP-literal hop.\nRegistries routes the Registry port by host and never falls through.\n\nThe control plane gains registries as integration state beside the Git\napplications'': records in the instance partition, credentials in the secret\nstore under a server-minted id, proven before recorded, audited, with their\nown errors and routes under /api/integrations/registries. The same router\nserves Platform Management. The console''s Integrations page gains an Image\nregistries section that shows what was proven, never \"connected\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: trigger existing security scans after targeting main\n\n* Reject credentials in blob redirects and test bounded registry reads\n\n* Apply pinned rustfmt layout to redirect fixture\n\n* Keep redirect redaction-test diagnostics free of secret values\n\n* State registry refusal and credential activation guarantees precisely\n\n* Count actual HTTP listing requests under challenge-based authentication\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: IngeniousRiley <336672273+IngeniousRiley@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3abb51342c0b6eb5bfd9de8ce94ede0ac3d57c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/e3abb51342c0b6eb5bfd9de8ce94ede0ac3d57c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/d28fc97d76f0319fb188b2d490149098e3db0a55","verification":{"payload":"tree e3abb51342c0b6eb5bfd9de8ce94ede0ac3d57c9\nparent e5d64987198ad07a4831510b1876f77df8f33e7a\nauthor Brett Smith <brett