hed to the component''s primary image and pushed last, so the\nimage a person selects carries the description of the software.\n\nOne rule, written once, decides whether a version is a release unit, and both\nPlatform Management''s discovery and the catalogue''s selection apply it.\nRegistries become operator-registered integrations: closed kinds, public\naddresses only, and credentials presented only to the repositories they were\nregistered for. The catalogue gains a described component kind that the\nserver resolves, and the save request can no longer carry what the server\nresolved. Fabric''s own release attaches its component descriptor, and the\nattach step lands only after every reader.\n\nPointer paragraphs record what this amends in ADRs 0008, 0021, 0023 and 0024.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Describe a component in one contract crate, and move the shapes it shares with the catalogue into it\n\nSlice 1 of ADR 0026. fabric-component, in neither plane and with no\ntransport, owns the component descriptor: its versioned envelope, a strict\nJSON reader that refuses duplicate keys and oversized documents before\nparsing, the repository, digest, role, name and version rules, a\ncanonical renderer from the authored component.yaml, and the\nPlatformCapability type. The configuration-field and application-resource\nshapes and their validators move into it from fabric-client-model, which\nre-exports them at their old paths; fixtures prove a catalogue and a client\ndocument re-render byte-identically, and every validator message is\nunchanged.\n\ncomponent.yaml describes saas-fabric by the three roles the platform already\npins. The release matrix gains each image''s role and marks runtime primary,\ninert until the attach job; a pull-request test renders component.yaml and\nchecks it against that matrix. Nothing is published.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: trigger existing security scans after targeting main\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: IngeniousRiley <336672273+IngeniousRiley@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwXNPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3kcQABxJ5M2InnGSFfwVrmZvaSaO\nivbQ5tNf+vpGPBQ/hWgbuErfsoDXDiRcb4Kruo4VsBi02RhEKJpJGvD2bTyr01Mg\n1jdrIClOpvhr4RXa0Ni/uBOZzFHYSiGDchHpDhOgUSOhzNTyoHALumtN93z4KJWq\n99T4tkzbxegevwLNd1cr26SNJQqUOr9nuCRn3nB+VzpOppe7KlzF9LvVI9JKZ0As\nU8pND4KGfu6bi9X/X5uv9LqH60FGO3kdENdWPPjO8BJCnioHqs8ox8Ttq36EX8XD\nFfC9JAA8IQoAitBptwCg1mrumjcFm20dkyjmli00AJTs25GcD1WB150MOTiRMQeY\ny3V7EC9NzjYABgQr4Z3LeD0ShAz7c+SR8aDhLKaAPCVoJvXypxPMTlHei0NlpxTj\nWfb42Q8436oIhPErZYebIvTKWRixPps54GjAIA8ufBJ2VjmG7vlnkQoX6WAgQr2L\nqsuCfj+JvJzTPMPbQ9Hu2Bi08BlZ4KADsDfZVPTU8qXwoQMBtwpSbitv89QaAK9n\nwx3qzoieW4q/1gc6CnBoy6HSc9oV8oAD2srZ3QlNCmnXNydViS5o/q0zkUPEiQZg\nnqJ+v0ko5QgqutvLwl1j6ge3J3jqR5e1tERJE1IDYTdsM6OaoIINSKDbpgNKLaBc\n4/hgP17HMBzuFm9XJcGQ\n=GvT8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T21:27:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/cdc4eab03c29bd35b925b0fc60772427261c43a6","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKGNkYzRlYWIwM2MyOWJkMzViOTI1YjBmYzYwNzcyNDI3MjYxYzQzYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928","sha":"461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928"}],"sha":"cdc4eab03c29bd35b925b0fc60772427261c43a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/cdc4eab03c29bd35b925b0fc60772427261c43a6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:02:18Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T21:02:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ADR 0026: a component describes itself in an artifact attached to its image, and the catalogue selects it from registries an operator registers (#94)\n\n* ADR 0026: a component describes itself in an artifact attached to its image, and the catalogue selects it from registries an operator registers\n\nA component publishes a component descriptor, a small JSON document naming\nits images by role and digest, the capabilities it needs, the configuration\nfields a client supplies and the Data API resources it exposes. It is an OCI\nartifact attached to the component''s primary image and pushed last, so the\nimage a person selects carries the description of the software.\n\nOne rule, written once, decides whether a version is a release unit, and both\nPlatform Management''s discovery and the catalogue''s selection apply it.\nRegistries become operator-registered integrations: closed kinds, public\naddresses only, and credentials presented only to the repositories they were\nregistered for. The catalogue gains a described component kind that the\nserver resolves, and the save request can no longer carry what the server\nresolved. Fabric''s own release attaches its component descriptor, and the\nattach step lands only after every reader.\n\nPointer paragraphs record what this amends in ADRs 0008, 0021, 0023 and 0024.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ADR 0026: say when LucentRoot''s OpenBao takes the External Secrets denial, and what holds until then\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ADR 0026: an anonymous proof ends at the challenge, and the per-component registry account lands with the picker\n\nGHCR''s realm refuses an anonymous token request for no scope while granting\nevery public repository, so a proof with no credential stops at a Bearer\nchallenge naming a realm the kind allows. Saying which registry each managed\ncomponent is read through needs the platform view to carry each component''s\nrepositories, which slice 4 adds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ADR 0026: the next version is the fix for a published one, and the version check fails closed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clarify descriptor rollout, credential and rollback gates\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: IngeniousRiley <336672273+IngeniousRiley@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8534df18ab835d449369d0bcd97488fa2624cb06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/8534df18ab835d449369d0bcd97488fa2624cb06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928","verification":{"payload":"tree 8534df18ab835d449369d0bcd97488fa2624cb06\nparent 8676af47867e694d4fe2fb4ea42c2d5ab2679376\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1791061338 +1300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791061338 +1300\n\nADR 0026: a component describes itself in an artifact attached to its image, and the catalogue selects it from registries an operator registers (#94)\n\n* ADR 0026: a component describes itself in an artifact attached to its image, and the catalogue selects it from registries an operator registers\n\nA component publishes a component descriptor, a small JSON document naming\nits images by role and digest, the capabilities it needs, the configuration\nfields a client supplies and the Data API resources it exposes. It is an OCI\nartifact attached to the component''s primary image and pushed last, so the\nimage a person selects carries the description of the software.\n\nOne rule, written once, decides whether a version is a release unit, and both\nPlatform Management''s discovery and the catalogue''s selection apply it.\nRegistries become operator-registered integrations: closed kinds, public\naddresses only, and credentials presented only to the repositories they were\nregistered for. The catalogue gains a described component kind that the\nserver resolves, and the save request can no longer carry what the server\nresolved. Fabric''s own release attaches its component descriptor, and the\nattach step lands only after every reader.\n\nPointer paragraphs record what this amends in ADRs 0008, 0021, 0023 and 0024.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ADR 0026: say when LucentRoot''s OpenBao takes the External Secrets denial, and what holds until then\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ADR 0026: an anonymous proof ends at the challenge, and the per-component registry account lands with the picker\n\nGHCR''s realm refuses an anonymous token request for no scope while granting\nevery public repository, so a proof with no credential stops at a Bearer\nchallenge naming a realm the kind allows. Saying which registry each managed\ncomponent is read through needs the platform view to carry each component''s\nrepositories, which slice 4 adds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ADR 0026: the next version is the fix for a published one, and the version check fails closed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Clarify descriptor rollout, credential and rollback gates\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: IngeniousRiley <336672273+IngeniousRiley@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwW1aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAID8QAJoYhTJMYTi4O4a1ECJcoXm9\n7vKaQ07xVZM53LJNJuUzozlgLwnK/6qN00Cf6dqVHacB/uhXpSoLi4GXSN14Be/Z\n+VUTJtgAwaST5FwD2zM50UEljm+ilHxagrdJwBV8flIxLS+wM9hEHatAqGD0yDhT\nn1Ro3Vlfr5OPLzXQ5QvpZ5V0rqPNO+x1eFdkzW9Vq7S5NbDaEc93sgtFWPTDs188\nh6+nxSirPRf+khNnp7mhj2XiCIoJzImc4GNCQ3b14YCGnefqFox38+M1t3Q+CAPU\n9ER1rV6+4ELvFCDx0GQ6iZPLqIR/kCmR9cWPBcA1Oz5EXusCev1YRmBLMwhAAhpC\n8wNeej5VjAOyYLvoOdJ4tF4eLhO7xQMjympYswFejeWthMcM2R2HGPpzGj1j0ZTD\n9tpCLfixzFz3Ivg6ABpWiXQQJ4cuqLdAjjLazLkZr7MCm47Mck7vTVgXOn70xWAv\nhEbrYNQKQkJEM2m2jHcLQ/dYDebxDt8q/3FMzPH+z5XMcxy1vZ1GKeK0lDlgXo6p\noRcNSkE4GxCXbWnWOO4neMTovUwaKUS093fDL1QQt1Pi1+8Y4mYTET55/J6ibNUZ\nNYawi4/XsmC2EijCabBnMYeW2aI+K97oscBvJP2otxES4aNoDW6sAILS0RsLbgsy\n/m2pF4WlMaA1SUvdCsJK\n=Pt/j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T21:02:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDQ2MWIyYTE3ZjY1YzgxOTk3M2NmMGE2YjdjYmFmOTdmZTQ1YWM5Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/8676af47867e694d4fe2fb4ea42c2d5ab2679376","sha":"8676af47867e694d4fe2fb4ea42c2d5ab2679376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/8676af47867e694d4fe2fb4ea42c2d5ab2679376"}],"sha":"461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/461b2a17f65c819973cf0a6b7cbaf97fe45ac928"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/8676af47867e694d4fe2fb4ea42c2d5ab2679376/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:11:41Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:11:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ADR 0025: say what state loss actually costs, and that the convergence is a Job, not a hook (#92)\n\nTwo sentences in the accepted ADR that the platform build''s review proved wrong: state loss is recovered by adoption, not by prevent_destroy; and the convergence is a Job whose health gates the next wave — Argo excludes hooks from an Application''s health, so a hook could not.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"28fdc6e9a14b8dc66d1aa960dcac9f63f4790008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/28fdc6e9a14b8dc66d1aa960dcac9f63f4790008"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/8676af47867e694d4fe2