eversed; the rule is enforced by a platform invariant. Amends ADR 0012 with a scope pointer and rewrites the control-plane architecture''s prerequisites as provisioned.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"9d53dbe547a263befe9096f63d60ee2d36739d2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/9d53dbe547a263befe9096f63d60ee2d36739d2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/ffb56e7b3002cce311994b0721304f8bde952ab8","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d53dbe547a263befe9096f63d60ee2d36739d2c\nparent 5320432978535fec8fd8f03ad6164f0656567edf\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1790054292 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790054292 +1200\n\nADR 0025: realm bootstrap is platform composition, done with the credential the platform generates (#91)\n\nAccepted by the product owner on 2026-09-22: nothing in the master realm is made by hand. The platform provisions the master realm''s instance resources with the bootstrap administrator credential it generates; the gateway''s secret is generated in-cluster and set on the client; operators are declared, not clicked; ADR 0012 is scoped, not reversed; the rule is enforced by a platform invariant. Amends ADR 0012 with a scope pointer and rewrites the control-plane architecture''s prerequisites as provisioned.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsg+UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOm8QABPHlCfzushfv+J04PAPPfjk\npMcqK/kRI1ucg2kSPHyM+u3xdMs89raCD9AYdK/WAwTDQugk3lNISPWT7Lc8WcY2\nq4f3/Mv54vZJaF1Vkkq4FO4kfwdBodxY4foZHzcbRQ9HyiKZYwbrq5UT5VUU7ti4\n57eMu/1RxRal6wGY2JjoG4b4kDEc/9gNadTZJdxKg7ssuSAlbKUZMTYM796ss3UE\nzUYnIfnF89OLG/Va7EsvVEGNfkeZsDX1mGzxicOIaa+H7IouCxUEiMsAyFc0UtA4\nNwbVHQLKNIhPtV8AoMn7Sl5keMHyD0Wcb1jKLyBaOQ4Kc37PWzkAd2YQDL+8gcHt\n+bdCICypjjTdsa4xfXUTRGMBFMNJ+8UoZmaAeO4j0eqkelgsBV4GX9Chl3V9xrMZ\nDzEVqQXaTJlqiF0RrMAF16n7ALhOU+JEcTb9q/I6Y2GkiHRtB1iYTDbFwm4NC5Xd\n3L5wyPfsUq4AEQQEZkGmQfkN3QpCOelh87kTY/rrbCimCkJd+jsVbhmDCwAuRkUL\nq7K7kgELVz8FSDTo/P4H9tudeP9pAtOO+tLQY+TEv9ZPf/u0mmyWYgfu5yNeKBaa\nxd7KWGLU22BHS8pHdjM5TTxoENiq6ONi+D9OuZxa7xjsGyK3gGTQT0I8H3hZyCyA\n0HomnQbyAhU45A0PR9LG\n=f85g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T05:18:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/ffb56e7b3002cce311994b0721304f8bde952ab8","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKGZmYjU2ZTdiMzAwMmNjZTMxMTk5NGIwNzIxMzA0ZjhiZGU5NTJhYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/5320432978535fec8fd8f03ad6164f0656567edf","sha":"5320432978535fec8fd8f03ad6164f0656567edf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/5320432978535fec8fd8f03ad6164f0656567edf"}],"sha":"ffb56e7b3002cce311994b0721304f8bde952ab8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/ffb56e7b3002cce311994b0721304f8bde952ab8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/5320432978535fec8fd8f03ad6164f0656567edf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:31:42Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T01:31:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Behind the gateway, the console uses the session it already has and never starts its own (#90)\n\nThe console''s half of ADR 0024 slice 1. Behind a gateway that runs the OIDC code flow and forwards the access token, the console probes GET /api/operator with cookies — after its own callback handling, before its silent sign-in — and on 200 is signed in with no token, no PKCE, nothing stored; on a 401 whose code is operator_refused it reports that the gateway signed the browser in but the control plane refused it, with no retry and no fall-through into its own flow; on any other 401 the standalone flow continues; anything else is a fault. Behind the gateway a 401 on a fetch navigates to / once per page load, remembering the operator''s place; the navigation is counted, cleared only by the first successful data call, and a third load that signs in and is refused is reported as looping. The control plane now tells a missing bearer (unauthenticated) from a refused one (operator_refused, a fixed sentence carrying nothing from the token), logged at the one funnel every refusal passes through and pinned by a tracing test; GET /api/operator documents the dependency and a router test pins the anonymous 401. Five adversarial rounds: the probe moved behind the callback so a probe failure cannot abandon a live code; the redirect bounded; the refused case surfaced by contract rather than comment; the log funnel made true; a first bound that cleared on the probe and never bound, rebuilt to clear on evidence. Ships before the platform''s gateway policy, which gives the gateway its own confidential client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"7b658dbf45603ea1e4aee43909b568adea738da2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/7b658dbf45603ea1e4aee43909b568adea738da2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/5320432978535fec8fd8f03ad6164f0656567edf","verification":{"payload":"tree 7b658dbf45603ea1e4aee43909b568adea738da2\nparent 2fe0ba0be69820f5e0e62025c3da75bab9c5a10b\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1790040702 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790040702 +1200\n\nBehind the gateway, the console uses the session it already has and never starts its own (#90)\n\nThe console''s half of ADR 0024 slice 1. Behind a gateway that runs the OIDC code flow and forwards the access token, the console probes GET /api/operator with cookies — after its own callback handling, before its silent sign-in — and on 200 is signed in with no token, no PKCE, nothing stored; on a 401 whose code is operator_refused it reports that the gateway signed the browser in but the control plane refused it, with no retry and no fall-through into its own flow; on any other 401 the standalone flow continues; anything else is a fault. Behind the gateway a 401 on a fetch navigates to / once per page load, remembering the operator''s place; the navigation is counted, cleared only by the first successful data call, and a third load that signs in and is refused is reported as looping. The control plane now tells a missing bearer (unauthenticated) from a refused one (operator_refused, a fixed sentence carrying nothing from the token), logged at the one funnel every refusal passes through and pinned by a tracing test; GET /api/operator documents the dependency and a router test pins the anonymous 401. Five adversarial rounds: the probe moved behind the callback so a probe failure cannot abandon a live code; the redirect bounded; the refused case surfaced by contract rather than comment; the log funnel made true; a first bound that cleared on the probe and never bound, rebuilt to clear on evidence. Ships before the platform''s gateway policy, which gives the gateway its own confidential client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsdp+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyRAQAE1XWj5PPlsZ+twXnGZ4tj3t\nEFWxdn74YvtrKkauixjk1Tu1kY5udGjOqU1DRyh1bHPXArvwdHdiA4RlVD/T9gK/\no/NZ1yeW/AlHnQOQyuWGdINDNCYKxhrWzicD8mU9zagtkj7QqKjmMUEEESdXIUtr\nwgk/1SLLj0uaUITUd6jh/X/MYSJHQSrFtapsSuRNOULazK6xeqh+XcTPZkuO/0Ti\n8aGDnmkD1d3ZGCXH2iPH8LCYMQ39p/nJixNEsLo5jOtx4x3mQKmYxtw9GfWWN0AM\n/x/yht+fxyVd1vOWgwyhy3KuBqRJABlX0D7F5gwe94UWP4hAoh4K1SfFNEb67eIP\nZ9SCWZscnVQ0xyI8oi38RF5Drk7DrSSyCXcRX2zfFLUu983lgy+KPE7Vm2VL9GvR\nmgX/jyNL1M5K0W/NdP3XOwn+IYx6X4u9W7S7AnlcS1qwSSjlcxBZevP8U7wlmVzk\nGooJ3fY0x3+1XbQtZyzILRabAGq/XOG8ud2lAMeiyXbjIGe2+LmeNyBzm6s7YYmE\nx4zRUSJYVfs0clwVoWaFzWrc/KxAwGCg0HAxrhdzxHwbXUd5isDpOAuKOr31qEpA\nlBEsPOivLfV1LOZb5cqU3F+9k3pqg2V9Hi77wlC9RvdMgSEOgwXUetHq0Lai/VDk\njzkfKblokazrsfqdhusd\n=eIPk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T01:31:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-fl