/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/2fe0ba0be69820f5e0e62025c3da75bab9c5a10b","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDJmZTBiYTBiZTY5ODIwZjVlMGU2MjAyNWMzZGE3NWJhYjljNWExMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/5f686f3668548085dba133f31936db1cc1d3e3e6","sha":"5f686f3668548085dba133f31936db1cc1d3e3e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/5f686f3668548085dba133f31936db1cc1d3e3e6"}],"sha":"2fe0ba0be69820f5e0e62025c3da75bab9c5a10b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/2fe0ba0be69820f5e0e62025c3da75bab9c5a10b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/5f686f3668548085dba133f31936db1cc1d3e3e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T20:25:57Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T20:25:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Run each operator-key refresh in its own task, so a panic in the realm adapter is logged and refresh continues (#88)\n\nThe operator signing-key refresh loop awaited the realm adapter directly on its own task, so a panic killed key refresh for the life of the process and every sign-in failed silently once the realm rotated. Each refresh now runs in its own task through the tick helper #83 placed for it, inside a span carrying the issuer on the panic line and on the two lines the refresh logs; a panic is logged as a fixed sentence, never its payload, and the next refresh proceeds after the usual interval; the warn-and-keep behaviour for an unreachable provider is unchanged. The loop moves to operator_keys/refresh.rs behind a crate-private SigningKeySource seam in refresh/source.rs — RealmSignIn::signing_keys is a concrete method with no trait, which is why nothing could test this loop before — implemented by the realm under a different method name so an upstream rename can never turn the delegation into recursion (an abort, which no guard could catch). The publication loop gains the same inner span so its skipped-pass warning carries the environment. Nothing in fabric-keycloak or fabric-control-plane changes. Adversarial review confirmed the direct-await mutation fails the test, that the visibility is the minimum Rust allows (a re-export cannot widen an item), and — with a standalone reproduction — that the inner span reaches both log lines.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"79bd68929392d68ea5370c96adde9f35cab10d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/79bd68929392d68ea5370c96adde9f35cab10d34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/5f686f3668548085dba133f31936db1cc1d3e3e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 79bd68929392d68ea5370c96adde9f35cab10d34\nparent 0453e9e35eac2f560b586312b508684cd8d35232\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1790022357 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790022357 +1200\n\nRun each operator-key refresh in its own task, so a panic in the realm adapter is logged and refresh continues (#88)\n\nThe operator signing-key refresh loop awaited the realm adapter directly on its own task, so a panic killed key refresh for the life of the process and every sign-in failed silently once the realm rotated. Each refresh now runs in its own task through the tick helper #83 placed for it, inside a span carrying the issuer on the panic line and on the two lines the refresh logs; a panic is logged as a fixed sentence, never its payload, and the next refresh proceeds after the usual interval; the warn-and-keep behaviour for an unreachable provider is unchanged. The loop moves to operator_keys/refresh.rs behind a crate-private SigningKeySource seam in refresh/source.rs — RealmSignIn::signing_keys is a concrete method with no trait, which is why nothing could test this loop before — implemented by the realm under a different method name so an upstream rename can never turn the delegation into recursion (an abort, which no guard could catch). The publication loop gains the same inner span so its skipped-pass warning carries the environment. Nothing in fabric-keycloak or fabric-control-plane changes. Adversarial review confirmed the direct-await mutation fails the test, that the visibility is the minimum Rust allows (a re-export cannot widen an item), and — with a standalone reproduction — that the inner span reaches both log lines.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsZLWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt38QAE2WANI1YASXaCNc9v8KaWRp\nKkTUW9DNqR8Jp3ys7E2pcpp+soqDLVTBJ17ZHzt7r//Z6sm2lpXwgywmqqzFzoSi\nr+P/Y8hvNUnjt3CAeNurpUh6/E+C2Z9bI6EKq4KBxXXinUyc1p7jwUcbjBrArPbv\na09DhJnvlfwkJQ7WsrbhdPMss3TPYRnaMwito/6GIOL6ng3r4uqrdQsdCJfpTE7+\nafxgcPqCdC1MC0VslbpQX2vh0zoJeJSfrMFvqtMus4AmU5SBCRgLLs/VW9jWf7fz\nG8051LEZvXGKPc0WBbWkqXC5HlZxFNTDZxyoUO546b+PqhPONghq8RwzBrTXtgpL\nGjfSQiIMLd9+QnCYSVsgwE8MLldAsprtgNG2+eArq4ppqUhwVJKxmQxU6maNaSj5\na3kgjaIabBbDmqxZD7qq3aNXF0i2zUvKEuO0vr0dzaGUit5HsW+5C4NGQcqivR7u\nZJNN0pAy80MQxijxGQAV/vEjkOxSG9gStN783dycDxzFnbIKCdYaINH8levy/wX3\nndI68iijKGz7WN8unMvPpxFnLB5bBG4g01P5kqAQ96MBnCCF9z8KlxbRj2WQMPjc\ntEla53eltmrVv00smmhA5jupcU/B5Po6acQSFlNMUUwxfDuNz+gZYJW9x1QH658w\nU92PjM+OS5C4BWv9KCEt\n=zvgk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T20:25:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https:/