://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/e38b6785c65c64e511b30d3351112067c15d7719","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKGUzOGI2Nzg1YzY1YzY0ZTUxMWIzMGQzMzUxMTEyMDY3YzE1ZDc3MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53","sha":"94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53"}],"sha":"e38b6785c65c64e511b30d3351112067c15d7719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/e38b6785c65c64e511b30d3351112067c15d7719"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T21:21:35Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T21:21:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Run each scheduled tick in its own task, so a panic in an adapter is logged and the loop continues (#83)\n\nThe platform sweep and runtime-publication loops in fabric-control-plane-api awaited each tick directly on the loop task, so a panic unwinding out of an adapter killed the loop for good — since #82 the running flag was released, but nothing ran again and the console''s Last check and Last pass silently stopped. Each tick now runs in its own task through one shared helper (startup/tick.rs, placed where the operator-key refresh loop can take it next): a panic comes back as a JoinError, is logged as a fixed sentence keyed control_plane.scheduled_pass_panicked inside a span carrying the environment — never the payload, which could carry a credential — and the loop continues; a tick still completes before the next one starts. start_publishing takes the platform config like start_sweeping does. Adversarial review found the pre-existing zero-interval test could not fail (a spawned task was never polled) and it now can; the change''s central property is pinned by a test-only tracing layer that records the panic event''s field names and values, which fails on a leaked payload in a field or in the message. Seven mutations are caught; thirty-plus repeat runs show no flake. Not fixed here: the operator-key refresh loop (filed), and recording a panicked pass on the console''s row.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"00f883de6e24476981f1127d0bb81df305089360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/00f883de6e24476981f1127d0bb81df305089360"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53","verification":{"payload":"tree 00f883de6e24476981f1127d0bb81df305089360\nparent 9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789939295 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789939295 +1200\n\nRun each scheduled tick in its own task, so a panic in an adapter is logged and the loop continues (#83)\n\nThe platform sweep and runtime-publication loops in fabric-control-plane-api awaited each tick directly on the loop task, so a panic unwinding out of an adapter killed the loop for good — since #82 the running flag was released, but nothing ran again and the console''s Last check and Last pass silently stopped. Each tick now runs in its own task through one shared helper (startup/tick.rs, placed where the operator-key refresh loop can take it next): a panic comes back as a JoinError, is logged as a fixed sentence keyed control_plane.scheduled_pass_panicked inside a span carrying the environment — never the payload, which could carry a credential — and the loop continues; a tick still completes before the next one starts. start_publishing takes the platform config like start_sweeping does. Adversarial review found the pre-existing zero-interval test could not fail (a spawned task was never polled) and it now can; the change''s central property is pinned by a test-only tracing layer that records the panic event''s field names and values, which fails on a leaked payload in a field or in the message. Seven mutations are caught; thirty-plus repeat runs show no flake. Not fixed here: the operator-key refresh loop (filed), and recording a panicked pass on the console''s row.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsE5fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEScQAB4FRwT0uz/XG+2lKKUPy1AC\n+bL2Rg2t/ZDi/W3jYuFeNoPJKE2h3NMFDfhqmR+puIMZVIB6rI1Bkb6vx8KM1pZK\nZgTSYKCCgRz1x0WWDlyq8xBNxoQ5DhTA1J2dLRn0/RNJcr2J6tFz9ij++0feu5Oh\n0fInjpHVQ8ntmVQ0/na+wy61Puo4iDkyStOrXqwBNs9NOn33o7PsA5+sDZRQeW2R\nz8kptWp7aR+5uksnNDgQZL3XeFZ2mUdzEJAEGKqVR4X6wzEZV6IvYmQxsOTTPmyi\nc0rKEZHqgCBc0UAzidsijM2JX+3eX/hwFTsK8cjrp3zE73h8ReTzSv5OwUcTBadi\nfpGoE86tYUndwz+VBhvDaCW9SXqM0FVW0DsNEIhs+PaxQuw+acIOnCm2bgyhQoaa\nHDohnbjyl9mfI6UU1Hx60iA0QE9AMASfDnCO4L/iUmwxRSfjsn9dDSvOrYM112rT\nr7ZK2pEFaI0WulIRKlcZ8AEXSMXD6/U6lTQ7HIl5bRkpVzbpq/25+A+KWAiWCqDe\nm0KSYpqsIkYpB+rIvcYi42ya/1oHT046UahiexqsmU8PwNiNI9mhfn/dXcCiQXyF\nOQsQUKmACFE+MfjU7h40cVnTecM1/8Cx62kv/WavTr9dsEHb6l0q9pdEI5kG2Z6X\nrj99gRFcJoVsN7cw+doy\n=OkSV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T21:21:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDk0NDY1Y2E4M2MwM2VkMzNiZjVhMjgwZThiMDVlNjU4OGU2YzFjNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a","sha":"9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a"}],"sha":"94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/94465ca83c03ed33bf5a280e8b05e6588e6c1c53"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:50:47Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:50:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pair the running flag''s swap with the guard that releases it, for the sweep as well as the publisher (#82)\n\nPlatformManagement::sweep set its running flag, awaited the sweep, cleared the flag with a plain store, and only then recorded what it found. A future dropped mid-sweep or a panic through an adapter skipped the store and left every later sweep answering AlreadyRunning — unreachable from today''s only caller, the scheduled loop, but one \"Check now\" trigger away. Releasing before recording also let a second sweep start, finish and record while the first had not yet written its older result, which then overwrote the newer one under a later timestamp. RunningGuard now lives once at the crate root and is obtainable only through RunningFlag::try_enter, which performs the swap and hands back the guard only when it won, so the swap and the guard cannot be separated and neither state''s flag is reachable from anywhere else; Drop releases it on every exit; the record sits under the guard; the publisher''s copy is deleted. Adversarial review drove the cancellation test to the publisher''s select!-on-one-task shape, tightened both panic tests to is_panic(), and produced the try_enter design; the guard replaced by a post-await store fails exactly the release tests, and reaching the inner bool around try_enter is a compile error. The loop body dying on a panic is a separate follow-up in fabric-control-plane-api.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"f974ad73850b92ad170af8c2329224de28be4a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/f974ad73850b92ad170af8c2329224de28be4a4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a","verification":{"payload":"tree f974ad73850b92ad170af8c2329224de28be4a4a\nparent 86ffc7b0a90330c991e73077a412503341c43b3e\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789897847 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789897847 +1200\n\nPair the running flag''s swap with the guard that releases it, for the sweep as well as the publisher (#82)\n\nPlatformManagement::sweep set its running flag, awaited the sweep, cleared the flag with a plain store, and only then recorded what it found. A future dropped mid-sweep or a panic through an adapter skipped the store and left every later sweep answering AlreadyRunning — unreachable from today''s only caller, the scheduled loop, but one \"Check now\" trigger away. Releasing before recording also let a second sweep start, finish and record while the first had not yet written its older result, which then overwrote the newer one under a later timestamp. RunningGuard now lives once at the crate root and is obtainable only through RunningFlag::try_enter, which performs the swap and hands back the guard only when it won, so the swap and the guard cannot be separated and neither state''s flag is reachable from anywhere else; Drop releases it on every exit; the record sits under the guard; the publisher''s copy is deleted. Adversarial review drove the cancellation test to the publisher''s select!-on-one-task shape, tightened both panic tests to is_panic(), and produced the try_enter design; the guard replaced by a post-await store fails exactly the release tests, and reaching the inner bool around try_enter is a compile error. The loop body dying on a panic is a separate follow-up in fabric-control-plane-api.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr6x3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQU4QAEUFAA2ekjJDFGpgGOp09V/4\nRracUVEoIdsB9y9mnR3gBoLk+2WFc7QJs+CbZccYsRkS0McKR7TwmaFVdDbb2lYU\nejgIAkdID3/TMKIOO6IcDK1huVWo2CHJY7YEZnuBFGawoi4rZdZsHY46jjdMuR8o\nauAJNF1gBT3LxukBkc+O5ZzbmD0sUDXQcNLhfcvHiOeh7Owd4ruyL5KvgrRlars+\nv4sgiHwTzxpkLZ47axzcoAMGo8dkDt7KLsbb4e6Ihh+1zFcHZ7ixoXMeBCnJbFEO\nxucbb2+xJySjcd90MyJLCOABIuFzqSN+UmZ/WP0CCqBOYP9vr/eMcK4XY6rxxS9W\nVtNDAD4+6JCpqrqBDobSMlJJFYNv9+loLeyFIrb4gP3bJ/e1v9mRcY1/4xRX1/7b\nuIydaqhnePlqlZEo87CSpWdo61htU5Ygd6KVr/jhRfi26Z0ea4O1377iJv8R7WgH\ntfbEQ4w1pnHja9acMx7NT19ep81GxQ04pmSsWdJdk2oySf0Q1VSnYfFKphU5K6Ki\nsxdmj6CEU0LF52Iz/YXv8EiGGwckm165CtF9FTHfrcsbU/oOdFsyPNEQZoWIn8FG\nG8GjaNN6g3KsC03BR1mqkV1IQY1aYLoMV2UCruIzt1CE43zWK6SOp1AYQ/kdkw0m\n7YnY7G9ZCkog0zG6AZYv\n=Fgcc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T09:50:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDlkNjkyNDA4NmFiNWQ1YTZlOTZjZjg2NmQ4MDNkNjFmN2M0MjQ1OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/86ffc7b0a90330c991e73077a412503341c43b3e","sha":"86ffc7b0a90330c991e73077a412503341c43b3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/86ffc7b0a90330c991e73077a412503341c43b3e"}],"sha":"9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/9d6924086ab5d5a6e96cf866d803d61f7c42458a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/86ffc7b0a90330c991e73077a412503341c43b3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:03:24Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:03:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Show the runtime-publication row on the Environments page, with Publish now (#81)\n\nThe console half of ADR 0023 slice 4. The Environments page gains a Runtime publication panel beneath the environment card: the target, the revision each of the three documents holds as of the last pass that published it or found it unchanged, and what that pass did, with a Publish now button that runs a pass immediately and renders the row the pass itself produced rather than reloading. It states what the target holds and what the last pass did and nothing about the runtime; null is \"not reported\", never zero; not configured is a sentence and no button; a pass already running is a role=\"status\" refusal, every other refusal a role=\"alert\"; one notice state, so a fault and a refusal can never render together; the success path is announced with the sanitised detail. waiting takes pending''s colour and refused takes failed''s. Adversarial review found the revision assertions unbound from their labels — a swapped row passed — and they are now bound and exact, with the swap, the neutral pill, null-as-zero and the dropped panel all proven to fail tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"052b197d946469a7cbb36a2c411816b1fce666a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/052b197d946469a7cbb36a2c411816b1fce666a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/86ffc7b0a90330c991e73077a412503341c43b3e","verification":{"payload":"tree 052b197d946469a7cbb36a2c411816b1fce666a5\nparent 840cc2abab846c775462236d950edd6b8a309732\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789895004 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789895004 +1200\n\nShow the runtime-publication row on the Environments page, with Publish now (#81)\n\nThe console half of ADR 0023 slice 4. The Environments page gains a Runtime publication panel beneath the environment card: the target, the revision each of the three documents holds as of the last pass that published it or found it unchanged, and what that pass did, with a Publish now button th