 a provisioner input as missing. All three exist since #78 and #79. The bullet now says what publication leaves to a person — raising the runtime, the connector list, the issuer-to-tenant registry — and that the console does not yet show the publication row, matching the control-plane architecture''s own \"still not built\" list under the anchor it links to.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"043a774d5e4bd6468f789eef9526a5879304abc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/043a774d5e4bd6468f789eef9526a5879304abc3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/840cc2abab846c775462236d950edd6b8a309732","verification":{"payload":"tree 043a774d5e4bd6468f789eef9526a5879304abc3\nparent de81b159652e10f75fc93f6d35bf23d7939d600c\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789872107 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789872107 +1200\n\nSay in the README what runtime publication now does, and what it still leaves to a person (#80)\n\nThe crate table already says the publisher controller calls `fabric-runtime-publication` (#79); the \"Not yet built\" list further down still said nothing calls it, and named a Kubernetes adapter, a scheduled caller and a provisioner input as missing. All three exist since #78 and #79. The bullet now says what publication leaves to a person — raising the runtime, the connector list, the issuer-to-tenant registry — and that the console does not yet show the publication row, matching the control-plane architecture''s own \"still not built\" list under the anchor it links to.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr0frCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnIgQAB0zZWXByGl5UvMvWsDBL1GV\niyH7nKpPtGF0ipg6b7q6YDnfAjinr6lSKR+iRs4+qw0piMEEw8W+gGpzWWXNOjKM\nTKG0SjS8NnVi48tm91lsLoKK4hx0KGFb421ex/6edIvrQkUTBaDJhsUBmVdSQqWt\nAWe+tw2EreNqms2lHU3xcYFLWprj0ZsqMD5vUus