23d7939d600c"}],"sha":"840cc2abab846c775462236d950edd6b8a309732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/840cc2abab846c775462236d950edd6b8a309732"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/de81b159652e10f75fc93f6d35bf23d7939d600c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:34:15Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:34:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Publish the runtime''s three documents from desired state, on a schedule and on demand (#79)\n\nThe controller half of ADR 0023 slice 4. On a schedule and on an operator''s request, the control plane composes the runtime''s three documents from the environment''s declared data sources, its recorded placements and the catalogue derived from published releases, and offers each to the publication target at the revision it holds; a document the target refuses as divergent is re-offered once, one revision higher, and only that one, so a revision advances only when its bytes did, and a pass that changes nothing writes nothing. An empty catalogue is reported as waiting and nothing is written. A placement record now carries a revision and a tenant''s binding revision is the sum of its records'' revisions. GET /api/platform gains a publication row that states what the last pass observed of the target and nothing about the runtime; POST /api/platform/publication runs a pass now; [platform_management.publication] names the namespace and the interval. Adversarial review fixes release the pass on cancellation and panic, keep repository detail out of the row, make the unconfigured deployment a 404, and classify adapter and held-file failures as ones the next pass repairs or ones a person must resolve. The platform repository''s Role, mounts and validator changes are saas-fabric-platform #40; its config section is draft #41, landing with the image advance.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"78c515291098fa82dc0c8f031b6d0419f9558722","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/78c515291098fa82dc0c8f031b6d0419f9558722"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/de81b159652e10f75fc93f6d35bf23d7939d600c","verification":{"payload":"tree 78c515291098fa82dc0c8f031b6d0419f9558722\nparent 77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789871655 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789871655 +1200\n\nPublish the runtime''s three documents from desired state, on a schedule and on demand (#79)\n\nThe controller half of ADR 0023 slice 4. On a schedule and on an operator''s request, the control plane composes the runtime''s three documents from the environment''s declared data sources, its recorded placements and the catalogue derived from published releases, and offers each to the publication target at the revision it holds; a document the target refuses as divergent is re-offered once, one revision higher, and only that one, so a revision advances only when its bytes did, and a pass that changes nothing writes nothing. An empty catalogue is reported as waiting and nothing is written. A placement record now carries a revision and a tenant''s binding revision is the sum of its records'' revisions. GET /api/platform gains a publication row that states what the last pass observed of the target and nothing about the runtime; POST /api/platform/publication runs a pass now; [platform_management.publication] names the namespace and the interval. Adversarial review fixes release the pass on cancellation and panic, keep repository detail out of the row, make the unconfigured deployment a 404, and classify adapter and held-file failures as ones the next pass repairs or ones a person must resolve. The platform repository''s Role, mounts and validator changes are saas-fabric-platform #40; its config section is draft #41, landing with the image advance.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqr0YnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfmIQADWAca4gN8Yfagc5TG1hdNn0\n1rIe0Z9Q+1roiOUWCOnZvOE2o0CRd4TVd7cEp7SOeNskNpTLN/3er6/pmICxC3Az\nc6c3o7+unvHD4yGpl5paSi8oN2dJvbc7aUb2FEeMbjIEh9rIIHUDCDjp8U068mXe\nRk5DLIXyONuzF9+0UXQ5IEqNORtOxOFd6DqlqfajqPyIIUTYXXThD6GJSpS1Ij8k\n1INquiAgeF+DBKzWr1PD5I5lQRW4LXEhYe42WmGL+HfifC1305mRPd0EQ6tq6kwL\nj9jML5IpJrqWm9ZZeiGq42O+iuE5Aeuo1Os0+B/hZ/JtB13ZlV5GFHYHrcORa8qH\nDTzu92dNT4TuboXVBM9CaW2yt7MV/ygStnp8dwfx7a3Fvtq1WNdwrfL4lkFGRYdf\neg+qW5r55cPPRronQ3nLlXmSfkaycuJH3rTeYqvanLZJjFsPjjFPlff7kKlYJNTf\n8pkz+G5q1Kzj7lO6yrDfcJQNHbrWw5/REsbz+OOCsbX/iCpnUKl4L28mij3hT2e3\nKxyUDpTCE2YjOj7zhrqsUrpDuhBXE4GHAItWDQZjviY8Z0TOZMbjeakd6/3E2Qst\nmT/F9Fk544ikuy+y/Mdc9OSA14ZO4tjmI9uKQzndLuPZs+0RUVLTuAHVsW2crB5V\nuyEAmlLHcOJF1JVzEKUo\n=rB02\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T02:34:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/de81b159652e10f75fc93f6d35bf23d7939d600c","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKGRlODFiMTU5NjUyZTEwZjc1ZmM5M2Y2ZDM1YmYyM2Q3OTM5ZDYwMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05","sha":"77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05"}],"sha":"de81b159652e10f75fc93f6d35bf23d7939d600c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/de81b159652e10f75fc93f6d35bf23d7939d600c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:27:12Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:27:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Decide a publication once, and publish it to the cluster as ConfigMaps (#78)\n\nThe groundwork half of slice 4 of ADR 0023, and the Kubernetes adapter ADR 0018 specified but did not build. fabric-runtime-publication exposes the decision its filesystem adapter used to make privately — HeldDocuments, plan_publication and PublicationPlan — so a second adapter cannot drift from the guards. fabric-publication-kubernetes implements the port over plain HTTPS the way the deployment observer does, with no kube crate, so ADR 0018''s open question about the workspace ban closes by precedent. Three ConfigMaps by ADR 0018''s names in one configured namespace; every object built and size-checked before any is written; replaces carry the version they were read at; nothing is ever deleted; errors name the document and never carry a body, a URL or the bearer. Proven against a fake API server, including byte equality with the filesystem adapter. The controller, the platform panel row, the operator trigger, and the platform repository''s Role and mounts are the other half.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"2a8467ea16c3d6e844ce4e444ebdf0cca8359a25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/2a8467ea16c3d6e844ce4e444ebdf0cca8359a25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a8467ea16c3d6e844ce4e444ebdf0cca8359a25\nparent 8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789860432 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789860432 +1200\n\nDecide a publication once, and publish it to the cluster as ConfigMaps (#78)\n\nThe groundwork half of slice 4 of ADR 0023, and the Kubernetes adapter ADR 0018 specified but did not build. fabric-runtime-publication exposes the decision its filesystem adapter used to make privately — HeldDocuments, plan_publication and PublicationPlan — so a second adapter cannot drift from the guards. fabric-publication-kubernetes implements the port over plain HTTPS the way the deployment observer does, with no kube crate, so ADR 0018''s open question about the workspace ban closes by precedent. Three ConfigMaps by ADR 0018''s names in one configured namespace; every object built and size-checked before any is written; replaces carry the version they were read at; nothing is ever deleted; errors name the document and never carry a body, a URL or the bearer. Proven against a fake API server, including byte equality with the filesystem adapter. The controller, the platform panel row, the operator trigger, and the platform repository''s Role and mounts are the other half.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrxpQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfh8QAKP7F+V4IeE7F+C2OmTseAH+\nSOpqshuiPZsnYaUGoQeyWAPAzxrAKVa6x/yuh1BfmO5tu/aRbgDvF9HTYKNYnJT5\nMuIbSvI/QEATMQXdV/h5Wo+3JY+sE