thub.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d"}],"sha":"77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/77c7bb05bcf699f069baf011005edf9fac846e05"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:23:16Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T23:23:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let an application declare its resources, and derive the runtime catalogue (#77)\n\nSlice 3 of ADR 0023. An application''s definition carries resources — the logical resources it exposes through the Data API, each with the wire''s own fields — edited on a Resources tab and carried by every release. GET /api/catalogue/runtime derives, from nothing stored, the catalogue the runtime would be given, and the Environments page shows it with the application and version each resource comes from. Newest published release wins per resource name; a name is owned by publication only, so a draft never blocks the rightful owner; a conflict produced by a hand edit is 500 desired_state_invalid and is never resolved by guessing. Proven through the real router: publish, derive, refuse a second owner naming both, supersede. Publishing to the runtime is slice 4.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"4890a387a4f9e517ca8e534146c5828a501788df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/4890a387a4f9e517ca8e534146c5828a501788df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4890a387a4f9e517ca8e534146c5828a501788df\nparent 12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789860196 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789860196 +1200\n\nLet an application declare its resources, and derive the runtime catalogue (#77)\n\nSlice 3 of ADR 0023. An application''s definition carries resources — the logical resources it exposes through the Data API, each with the wire''s own fields — edited on a Resources tab and carried by every release. GET /api/catalogue/runtime derives, from nothing stored, the catalogue the runtime would be given, and the Environments page shows it with the application and version each resource comes from. Newest published release wins per resource name; a name is owned by publication only, so a draft never blocks the rightful owner; a conflict produced by a hand edit is 500 desired_state_invalid and is never resolved by guessing. Proven through the real router: publish, derive, refuse a second owner naming both, supersede. Publishing to the runtime is slice 4.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrxlkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWK0QAAuYKWGgId1KvlbGOnnVDpKk\ncm47CEwBcwArC4iAG2cl5cXid6vjP2Hiq2RAcC+S1ThHmbx7zpqGzard12XXJLNT\n/yTzT3IcFL8EXeeioqDDe5LhRCS9zeU654bkT7ZF1mqjO4pN0ikqrGF0JqdPQ4Lf\nXWZy2NZOlWdSpOHWreLcvVNINXbphb4OcpWZl7xhLameRTAFEYeWJ4wwwBJQXmmh\newax7dHAFVBhKsw9Z0wSpmUF1MFwFVuTQkCPVi4YxlmBm4W5MPSS+FHXzER2gbfJ\n1/RdiSlAFBlI1r0TXbqVEQRIzSRH3h7XzF34OwalmfLjyjNfm8Tt9m8w+v3ZiY1Y\nCdaVvidQ4P5sV1+QxV6oi9VRsSo/k7SQCmNBDp9KjHbsaA/KasvT8twS6CAsk9BE\nJJ33Vb7zDauI7Ib8VKoUbSYl2JbsbVL1jXctL6+dj/GrNh1HgSWsK0kht+r9CaEM\n14vR0P22pMy5lsnNKSTxkYSvoR3nc2qrui696SYvDD+zIYQZVGetJDvsy/HBtgyL\nv5N61iJ/B4ndL7AB5Fy3JQ4BWSg6gox/XCNuVuYMTaemgaxaHcFLAwoFomC8Jkdk\nAUD7npOneDqyx/CdDzpp2nv8AmzhndhhBJod+35K6OJw4DQLotuIpw6khFwqvhGh\n5rd93ks28WYtGJsqRefb\n=QWXN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T23:23:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDhmZmUwZjQ2MjJhOWEwMWJmNTQxODk5YzBiYmMzMGU1ZDg0MzdjOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0","sha":"12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0"}],"sha":"8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/8ffe0f4622a9a01bf541899c0bbc30e5d8437c9d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:13:00Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:13:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Place a client''s data on a declared source, and record the placement (#76)\n\nThe second slice of ADR 0023 (Proposed). A client''s spec.data is now typed\nintent — class, provider, region — and an operator places each logical data\nsource on a declared one from the client''s new Data tab. Fabric selects the\nsource, allocates the tenant''s isolation, and records the outcome in\nenvironments/<environment>/placements.yaml beside the data sources, so that\npublication copies a fact rather than recomputing a guess (ADR 0007, ADR\n0018). A break-glass edit to the record is honoured as written.\n\nThe selector is pure and is the only thing that decides. A shared source\ntakes the tenant on its declared discriminator column with the tenant id as\nthe value: unique by construction, recorded once, never derived again. Any\nother class means one tenant per source with whole-database isolation;\nschema isolation is never produced (ADR 0006). A refusal names what would\nhave to be declared, and a stated provider is carried but not matched,\nbecause nothing declares one yet.\n\nPlacing and removing each write two documents in one commit, at the\nrevisions they were read. Without that, a placement recorded between a\nremoval''s read and its write leaves the environment naming a source nothing\ndeclares, and every later read fails. Held records are validated on every\nread: a duplicate, a dangling source, an isolation that disagrees with the\nsource''s class or column, two tenants on one discriminator value, or two\nwhole-database tenants on one source, and the environment says so.\n\nRoutes: GET /api/clients/{id}/placements, POST\n/api/clients/{id}/placements/{logical}, DELETE\n/api/platform/data-sources/{id}, each behind the operator and each\npreconditioned on the revision the operator read. The HTTP-surface test\ndrives the real router through a real PlatformDesiredState.\n\nNot here, deliberately: unplacing a tenant (ADR 0021''s deprovisioning\nquestion), automatic placement (the publisher''s controller, slice 4), and\nprovisioning a database for a dedicated intent when none is declared.\n\nVerified locally with every CI gate. Three adversarial reviews ran; every\nblocking finding is resolved here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cafc617373bb033273c30bdceeb28faaffe7295f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/cafc617373bb033273c30bdceeb28faaffe7295f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0","verification":{"payload":"tree cafc617373bb033273c30bdceeb28faaffe7295f\nparent f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789704780 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789704780 +1200\n\nPlace a client''s data on a declared source, and record the placement (#76)\n\nThe second slice of ADR 0023 (Proposed). A client''s spec.data is now typed\nintent — class, provider, region — and an operator places each logical data\nsource on a declared one from the client''s new Data tab. Fabric selects the\nsource, allocates the tenant''s isolation, and records the outcome in\nenvironments/<environment>/placements.yaml beside the data sources, so that\npublication copies a fact rather than recomputing a guess (ADR 0007, ADR\n0018). A break-glass edit to the record is honoured as written.\n\nThe selector is pure and is the only thing that decides. A shared source\ntakes the tenant on its declared discriminator column with the tenant id as\nthe value: unique by construction, recorded once, never derived again. Any\nother class means one tenant per source with whole-database isolation;\nschema isolation is never produced (ADR 0006). A refusal names what would\nhave to be declared, and a stated provider is carried but not matched,\nbecause nothing declares one yet.\n\nPlacing and removing each write two documents in one commit, at the\nrevisions they were read. Without that, a placement recorded between a\nremoval''s read and its write leaves the environment naming a source nothing\ndeclares, and every later read fails. Held records are validated on every\nread: a duplicate, a dangling source, an isolation that disagrees with the\nsource''s class or column, two tenants on one discriminator value, or two\nwhole-database tenants on one source, and the environment says so.\n\nRoutes: GET /api/clients/{id}/placements, POST\n/api/clients/{id}/placements/{logical}, DELETE\n/api/platform/data-sources/{id}, each behind the operator and each\npreconditioned on the revision the operator read. The HTTP-surface test\ndrives the real router through a real PlatformDesiredState.\n\nNot here, deliberately: unplacing a tenant (ADR 0021''s deprovisioning\nquestion), automatic placement (the publisher''s controller, slice 4), and\nprovisioning a database for a dedicated intent when none is declared.\n\nVerified locally with every CI gate. Three adversarial reviews ran; every\nblocking finding is resolved here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrLpMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzDgQAGzI0OY2nf6gSXPFdW1lQ3XM\n8pEkp7k5nMDQAyx0VPJ2xydZR4sjDho+gphhu9T0oCEsdU+oIw2nGVte1FKuZc+O\n3PXW6Myh0OKijIp1GRCrY8Kb6B2JDGpyWU0AMB/KY5Rir/f+DcfXhiad49WbxhxO\nsXB4N536ZURlg5A9SVCeQeUxCelil4+qfHxkVTIVQ/0OFL+OUcBFwZshrYTqLC/T\nwv3r66X4ejnh1aBFe+1C7xmQn2RaKj4MojOToouxTB24XbL28qFKbsmrhbG42AjQ\nUmKlDGAEyCY/qzjhg6PWxL2lokEWRAn9xh284txa/ivEnrve/IHUZSGp7J2vg8r5\n6kfrlAidwodQbGDTrSTaJfhKFLeULU+2URN4vyipJQoP85hWa7fUvXWzqUWvZXef\nfvQWiKTM6ksGOl3de/XSEcaitG/GAF1AZeUbiMjq6uem2494Xrk6IJ+d5SQ1NLWn\nTziplMi93f0QEQ04J38jir+TcC+6dcofW0kOEcA+jWEeIirDs6eTMTnBeUrXbTrm\nTWXpmVlXUNlpHiRDRhbpx3RA3c1WIZjD/vW1Kvw5XKPsOH/wc5LOu6k4AmNB3juF\nLZ19g5w+b1knJCwn3mWfBCzIdA22FQmhbA5pLttFkizrfdf99jpW1pvklrB6kb4S\nQ7avvYV0iKaUlwZ5tWjD\n=GAgC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T04:13:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDEyZjZmNGUxM2Q2Y2I1MDIyOTFhMDM1OWI3ODdkZWM0OWM4YjQyZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de","sha":"f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de"}],"sha":"12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/12f6f4e13d6cb502291a0359b787dec49c8b42f0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:41:49Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:41:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Declare an environment''s data sources in the product, as desired state (#75)\n\nThe first slice of ADR 0023 (Proposed): a data source is environment\ndesired state, declared from the console and written by Fabric to\nenvironments/<environment>/data-sources.yaml in the platform repository,\nbeside components.yaml and through the same GitHub App, one commit per\nchange. It is the first input the runtime''s published documents need that\nnothing yet produced, and the first step on the path that serves a tenant on\nLucentRoot without anyone hand-authoring the runtime''s documents.\n\nWhat this settles, and what it deliberately does not:\n\n- Each declared entry is built from the wire contract''s own sub-types\n  (ADR 0018), spelled as the wire spells them, so the file cannot disagree\n  with what will be published from it. The one field the wire leaves to the\n  tenant binding, the discriminator column, is declared once on the shared\n  source that carries it (ADR 0006) and copied to tenants when they are\n  placed. Placement, the derived runtime catalogue and the publisher are the\n  next three slices of the same decision.\n- The late-bound binding holds one adapter that implements both ports,\n  through a PlatformRepository trait; the rules and the component sweep keep\n  their narrow DesiredState view. The binding always has a fact to\n  compare-and-swap on, the generation tag, even before the file exists, so a\n  create decided against one repository cannot land on another after a\n  rebind. The API therefore always answers a revision and always requires\n  If-Match: the \"no revision yet\" branch production could never take is not\n  in the contract.\n- Validation refuses at declaration what the runtime would refuse later: a\n  shared source without a discriminator column, any other placement with\n  one, a zero pool, an empty label, a malformed secret reference, and the\n  wire''s undeclarable default connection. A hand-broken file (a duplicate\n  id, an entry that fails a rule) is answered as invalid desired state, not\n  as a retryable outage; a refused credential still is.\n- Nothing is deleted, published, or placed. Removal arrives with placement,\n  where the reference check lives.\n\nRoutes: GET /api/platform/data-sources, PUT /api/platform/data-sources/{id},\nboth behind the operator, with the catalogue path''s precondition handling\nreused rather than re-implemented. The HTTP-surface test drives the real\nrouter through a real PlatformDesiredState, as docs/delivery.md requires.\n\nVerified locally with every CI gate: fmt, clippy and rustdoc with -D\nwarnings, the workspace tests (2169 passing), cargo deny, the file-size,\ntoolchain-pin and architecture checks, and the console''s lint, typecheck,\n177 tests and build. Three adversarial reviews and a closure check ran over\nthe change; every blocking finding is resolved here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"796856ce5ae7b5a0b80156ae3a7dd6274f519e43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/796856ce5ae7b5a0b80156ae3a7dd6274f519e43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de","verification":{"payload":"tree 796856ce5ae7b5a0b80156ae3a7dd6274f519e43\nparent 0041d51b35926497b08896ecd1cd30e53761010d\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789695709 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789695709 +1200\n\nDeclare an environment''s data sources in the product, as desired state (#75)\n\nThe first slice of ADR 0023 (Proposed): a data source is environment\ndesired state, declared from the console and written by Fabric to\nenvironments/<environment>/data-sources.yaml in the platform repository,\nbeside components.yaml and through the same GitHub App, one commit per\nchange. It is the first input the runtime''s published documents need that\nnothing yet produced, and the first step on the path that serves a tenant on\nLucentRoot without anyone hand-authoring the runtime''s documents.\n\nWhat this settles, and what it deliberately does not:\n\n- Each declared entry is built from the wire contract''s own sub-types\n  (ADR 0018), spelled as the wire spells them, so the file cannot disagree\n  with what will be published from it. The one field the wire leaves to the\n  tenant binding, the discriminator column, is declared once on the shared\n  source that carries it (ADR 0006) and copied to tenants when they are\n  placed. Placement, the derived runtime catalogue and the publisher are the\n  next three slices of the same decision.\n- The late-bound binding holds one adapter that implements both ports,\n  through a PlatformRepository trait; the rules and the component sweep keep\n  their narrow DesiredState view. The binding always has a fact to\n  compare-and-swap on, the generation tag, even before the file exists, so a\n  create decided against one repository cannot land on another after a\n  rebind. The API therefore always answers a revision and always requires\n  If-Match: the \"no revision yet\" branch production could never take is not\n  in the contract.\n- Validation refuses at declaration what the runtime would refuse later: a\n  shared source without a discriminator column, any other placement with\n  one, a zero pool, an empty label, a malformed secret reference, and the\n  wire''s undeclarable default connection. A hand-broken file (a duplicate\n  id, an entry that fails a rule) is answered as invalid desired state, not\n  as a retryable outage; a refused credential still is.\n- Nothing is deleted, published, or placed. Removal arrives with placement,\n  where the reference check lives.\n\nRoutes: GET /api/platform/data-sources, PUT /api/platform/data-sources/{id},\nboth behind the operator, with the catalogue path''s precondition handling\nreused rather than re-implemented. The HTTP-surface test drives the real\nrouter through a real PlatformDesiredState, as docs/delivery.md requires.\n\nVerified locally with every CI gate: fmt, clippy and rustdoc with -D\nwarnings, the workspace tests (2169 passing), cargo deny, the file-size,\ntoolchain-pin and architecture checks, and the console''s lint, typecheck,\n177 tests and build. Three adversarial reviews and a closure check ran over\nthe change; every blocking finding is resolved here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrJbdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+koQAHkri9RZQmGXVP3+gqKkJOrs\nq3SVTH77hHrJK/CDVwNVcPclYPOmoa8CS9Ysh4re4bRWtRubQytLA5l6N0LTKW2p\nS4D2XADw+1qn/9oQ3G/RS8DlW5PrZtmDI39o2DlmNhLlsxtbmkxq4bdaPOMuHwIR\nXfniRQWre/TXo90HRAxbi5K/uGNLmAllZBNogKBhUM6Hi6Nnn2a16169H9f1Yutm\nsaGayVlPJkjCZCKUyY9lOtXelhv6y07QRMJepyEwgql8+E9q4lKX02xsr5r/d4um\ngofAwUxnvrThqKAnO5yXI7b8KejfySaMDq/ICF/c4zDqH9sRlwdEKqw+GIjZXB9V\nN5dFqjKZHXQ92XmBUZE8Ng9dPo4W39v+HQh8QjVM+bZ70Nx4ZI3DItGW9owBYXd4\nLip5GF7HEZrV7T4bC7qGX54Hfr32pz6eGwTbrFoOLS5inhbERXGhhHelmqnkKYHk\nS/x8RITKDWQrfwRrfaKcV+9PJjqTPYwuGpBIjuKwDlA/tvhUDNmvic7d5eoJUyM/\n6U1l5v6cekHzry1MbqdVFSWc7d8To4YpSnv4PS0tHahXEBwXMbTStjVJ8sYsplsr\nFmEJAxkAphnTpPczMpcP5PmeAYTA3NJryrD1GRx7aF+TDd4/UULE/0Ynj4nYedLj\n8n8kZTiepVDueIWtQDVp\n=gpUl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T01:41:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKGY5ZDQzMTFlMTA4YmJlMzdjZDVkMjhmNGRhZGUyZWFkOTg1NTc5ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/0041d51b35926497b08896ecd1cd30e53761010d","sha":"0041d51b35926497b08896ecd1cd30e53761010d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/0041d51b35926497b08896ecd1cd30e53761010d"}],"sha":"f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/f9d4311e108bbe37cd5d28f4dade2ead985579de"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/0041d51b35926497b08896ecd1cd30e53761010d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T22:28:01Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T22:28:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Say what is built, for every crate, before tagging v0.3.0 (#74)\n\nThe documentation had fallen behind the code by ten pull requests. This\nbrings every top-level claim back to what the tree at f4a39d1 does, and\ngives the nine crates that had no developer documentation the same\nREADME.md and CONTEXT.md pair every other crate carries.\n\nWhat changed, and what proved it:\n\n- README.md lists all 23 crates in the plane scripts/check_architecture.py\n  assigns each to, with an \"In neither plane\" group for the six that sit\n  beside fabric-core. \"Status\" and \"Not yet built\" now say that OIDC\n  sign-in, in-product Git connection, Platform Management with observed\n  running versions (ADR 0022), client secrets, the product catalogue (#69),\n  keyed writes (#71) and the authorization front door are built, and that\n  the runtime-publication caller, the provisioner input, the other\n  reconciliation targets, deprovisioning and application deployment are\n  not. The \"never calls a platform service\" claim is scoped to identity.\n- Nine new crate doc pairs: fabric-api, fabric-fga-auth, fabric-fga-auth-api,\n  fabric-openbao, fabric-git-host, fabric-platform-git,\n  fabric-platform-management, fabric-registry, fabric-deployment-kubernetes.\n  Every public item, route, key, variant and test name was checked against\n  the source; drafts that predated #72 were corrected for the observer port.\n- docs/verification.md is re-run on 2026-09-18: 2098 tests, 23 crates, the\n  dependency graph rebuilt from the architecture check''s own table, F3\n  recorded as closed by #71, and the Git-host bullets distinguishing \"no\n  automated test\" from what was observed on real hosts, with the command.\n- Two stale rustdoc claims corrected: fabric-fga-auth does call the\n  authorization service it embeds; fabric-openbao implements three ports.\n  The operator_keys and routes comments no longer describe the removed\n  trusted-header posture, and neither does examples/control-plane.toml.\n- The console''s dev proxy no longer injects a Tailscale-User-Login header\n  the control plane stopped reading when OIDC became the only posture; the\n  loopback workbench has its own proxy and is unchanged.\n- examples/authorization.toml gains the drift test the README already\n  claimed every example had, through the crate''s real loader.\n- Cargo.toml''s repository URL names the FieldstateNZ organisation; the\n  Dockerfile counts twenty-three crates; packaging.md and the README say the\n  authorization-front target exists and is not yet published.\n\nTwo adversarial reviews ran over this change; their twelve blocking\nfindings are all resolved here, including a port-to-crate mapping that was\nbackwards, a key cache described as interval-driven that is demand-driven,\nand four crates the dependency graph had placed in the wrong plane.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"74bab9339ef6475d8f0480b567a1b76d0af0caca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/74bab9339ef6475d8f0480b567a1b76d0af0caca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/0041d51b35926497b08896ecd1cd30e53761010d","verification":{"payload":"tree 74bab9339ef6475d8f0480b567a1b76d0af0caca\nparent f4a39d1c804abd3ebb329f55d05a0317e0c7b098\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789684081 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789684081 +1200\n\nSay what is built, for every crate, before tagging v0.3.0 (#74)\n\nThe documentation had fallen behind the code by ten pull requests. This\nbrings every top-level claim back to what the tree at f4a39d1 does, and\ngives the nine crates that had no developer documentation the same\nREADME.md and CONTEXT.md pair every other crate carries.\n\nWhat changed, and what proved it:\n\n- README.md lists all 23 crates in the plane scripts/check_architecture.py\n  assigns each to, with an \"In neither plane\" group for the six that sit\n  beside fabric-core. \"Status\" and \"Not yet built\" now say that OIDC\n  sign-in, in-product Git connection, Platform Management with observed\n  running versions (ADR 0022), client secrets, the product catalogue (#69),\n  keyed writes (#71) and the authorization front door are built, and that\n  the runtime-publication caller, the provisioner input, the other\n  reconciliation targets, deprovisioning and application deployment are\n  not. The \"never calls a platform service\" claim is scoped to identity.\n- Nine new crate doc pairs: fabric-api, fabric-fga-auth, fabric-fga-auth-api,\n  fabric-openbao, fabric-git-host, fabric-platform-git,\n  fabric-platform-management, fabric-registry, fabric-deployment-kubernetes.\n  Every public item, route, key, variant and test name was checked against\n  the source; drafts that predated #72 were corrected for the observer port.\n- docs/verification.md is re-run on 2026-09-18: 2098 tests, 23 crates, the\n  dependency graph rebuilt from the architecture check''s own table, F3\n  recorded as closed by #71, and the Git-host bullets distinguishing \"no\n  automated test\" from what was observed on real hosts, with the command.\n- Two stale rustdoc claims corrected: fabric-fga-auth does call the\n  authorization service it embeds; fabric-openbao implements three ports.\n  The operator_keys and routes comments no longer describe the removed\n  trusted-header posture, and neither does examples/control-plane.toml.\n- The console''s dev proxy no longer injects a Tailscale-User-Login header\n  the control plane stopped reading when OIDC became the only posture; the\n  loopback workbench has its own proxy and is unchanged.\n- examples/authorization.toml gains the drift test the README already\n  claimed every example had, through the crate''s real loader.\n- Cargo.toml''s repository URL names the FieldstateNZ organisation; the\n  Dockerfile counts twenty-three crates; packaging.md and the README say the\n  authorization-front target exists and is not yet published.\n\nTwo adversarial reviews ran over this change; their twelve blocking\nfindings are all resolved here, including a port-to-crate mapping that was\nbackwards, a key cache described as interval-driven that is demand-driven,\nand four crates the dependency graph had placed in the wrong plane.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrGlxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAasMQAC31gV9hZ/Op89fwNaFdwXtZ\nBTNwZpkIJV0WrncericMHOIs7S7RZQhSPpJvG79tlVaJGnnyyRFtclwhOhHBaLOi\nqopDdkASOYAnbC3NzAFDoCN4yuvnSf9ZT2yKS+Kkn8j9f1KgvPy1IBtDuwLyjdzj\nR3AtL47loLIe3Ge401IsIvr25Kux3uVQgJJLFWEahCy0pj3COKekXgAYsTx39nSP\nBstVG8tLBOmDRlFFOGRHZ3rj3/x952pScLW4Vks0CY9+cOsDLEHCOClVSSEdWOHS\nyILa6qOwLPOz9fGvjxPMIlm5r2O+ewLv+oS13eI8tUbKyafLjNXR3MjsAxoUm5BA\nwoXHQPkKzq9MuXmZCr/ORu3YESw0MKlLGA6aV8YGwwlJ2EFyb+npDFmUgj7jmUc8\n2y7n9t2PYaCj7fKOl8g7OHpmrsaP1Z4B0QYns1cY+wKNsR19EmploOLpaYR58TXM\nHTkG1b/B24sidJo1T