ion whose release snapshots are projected into identity as public PKCE clients; operator activity; a persistent local development repository; and a loopback workbench. ADR 0021 (Proposed) records the decisions this makes and the seven still owed. Review fixes refuse a client that would take over a reserved or already-declared realm, keep reconciliation observations out of desired state, version the catalogue document, bound documents below the Git contents API''s read ceiling while leaving identity edits room for remediation, give unreadable stored data, taken ids and lost races their own errors, audit every write, and stop a double-click or a held Enter from creating a client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"ff2a042532564ceb5e6779afb77e41d81ab6f3f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/ff2a042532564ceb5e6779afb77e41d81ab6f3f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/69dc8a7fc561bbb21b2c57e13a5929fc3c1b2017","verification":{"payload":"tree ff2a042532564ceb5e6779afb77e41d81ab6f3f6\nparent 72aac20b7693cb5448874b7f3baf85c71c8bb61d\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789622756 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789622756 +1200\n\nBuild the phase-one operator console and its persistent product workflows (#69)\n\nBuilds the phase-one operator application: a console following the v2 prototype; a product catalogue as versioned desired state, with application drafts, immutable numbered releases, components, features, plans, typed client fields and navigation; client creation; per-client product configuration whose release snapshots are projected into identity as public PKCE clients; operator activity; a persistent local development repository; and a loopback workbench. ADR 0021 (Proposed) records the decisions this makes and the seven still owed. Review fixes refuse a client that would take over a reserved or already-declared realm, keep reconciliation observations out of desired state, version the catalogue document, bound documents below the Git contents API''s read ceiling while leaving identity edits room for remediation, give unreadable stored data, taken ids and lost races their own errors, audit every write, and stop a double-click or a held Enter from creating a client.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq3nkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZP0QADSoi1oJ4dzzwkg+g3LEyRtg\n8Jly16FTTbm0EQ0ueY7ZDzStfwK5I7I2sMOii2U3SdeXHwfHQ7i44za5h5MJEDg7\n4mUlLLPgy5FMoahNwBdd7rQPY48BG1pePmG6ruFRbi/Fe4p6Pu38QeHLpuBmyPvk\nydJl1e7bkQ5BOYjo6fNj9DwyJbTrCs4VBrq9Xryf2mHZRwq6mfrihvs5YX5dqWyN\n+Ra1NeeANO9b/JBLxh4l8nlZRVBsevFeH4FMOF9TCpDHxE8Lam+3XyS+Aolc5Mti\ns0NWX2nlMakB4Iec74twTQUxnLLJ4N3pmRzKd1zNQD6EtNIf+4Xkbvs3LH1SNCuK\nPAvGs7g3oqKSn7twY4hXnDQip3b+vTA7X+wSMBjSnZLN+ovzRLWxM0LrNsN0YBJn\nhj/OwLhrJrDu2BFW4xHoBnSI+lsUaX5ecIgChSZNtwDaru7ZgdrJQl1EO4xFHuZ5\nyj6tWJCIkU9om7PW17tsnkRSe8UVd20h4Vn5O4Lp9+Hape/DeW1DP6EeAuKdTnAu\nNKCp6tiu+focCl5RVRSc5VcIwUynmsCbR0xfYcObcedLmezBbpiwalNNMZBVN51a\nDXrijZ9h7HSi+mWji46ps9pjV0prDcmiyMj6otDDSQ8eaztsgdXBHSnHgKzl7JWx\nvbcK3dVuu3q7GCI8aHkN\n=VAos\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T05:25:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/69dc8a7fc561bbb21b2c57e13a5929fc3c1b2017","node_id":"C_kwDOT19v0doAKDY5ZGM4YTdmYzU2MWJiYjIxYjJjNTdlMTNhNTkyOWZjM2MxYjIwMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commit/72aac20b7693cb5448874b7f3baf85c71c8bb61d","sha":"72aac20b7693cb5448874b7f3baf85c71c8bb61d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/72aac20b7693cb5448874b7f3baf85c71c8bb61d"}],"sha":"69dc8a7fc561bbb21b2c57e13a5929fc3c1b2017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/69dc8a7fc561bbb21b2c57e13a5929fc3c1b2017"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/commits/72aac20b7693cb5448874b7f3baf85c71c8bb61d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T05:13:09Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T05:13:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let a keyed update or delete reach a real ndc-postgres procedure, and close ADR 0004 (#71)\n\nCloses #67. A procedure mapping may now name which arguments carry the logical key and how an update payload is shaped, so a keyed update or delete reaches ndc-postgres v3.1.0''s real primary-key-scoped procedures. ADR 0020 supersedes ADR 0004: key values come only from direct equalities in the tenant-scoped predicate, never from the request body; the discriminator reaches the procedure twice; the full predicate still goes out under filter_argument; and startup refuses any required argument a verb''s translation does not send. Proven against a real connector, including a delete scoped to another tenant leaving the row untouched. Adversarial review fixes refuse a key that would displace the predicate, make the startup check verb-aware, refuse a payload on a delete, and pin that a key never falls back to the body. Also moves rustls to 0.23.45 for RUSTSEC-2026-0285.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"48eba54230cd058d82be81546983847df09391bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/trees/48eba54230cd058d82be81546983847df09391bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/saas-fabric/git/commits/72aac20b7693cb5448874b7f3baf85c71c8bb61d","verification":{"payload":"tree 48eba54230cd058d82be81546983847df09391bf\nparent 34b5c5f8d8778ac1c6537fe7ab2b63a0f1d5e3c7\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1789621989 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789621989 +1200\n\nLet a keyed update or delete reach a real ndc-postgres procedure, and close ADR 0004 (#71)\n\nCloses #67. A procedure mapping may now name which arguments carry the logical key and how an update payload is shaped, so a keyed update or delete reaches ndc-postgres v3.1.0''s real primary-key-scoped procedures. ADR 0020 supersedes ADR 0004: key values come only from direct equalities in the tenant-scoped predicate, never from the request body; the discriminator reaches the procedure twice; the full predicate still goes out under filter_argument; and startup refuses any required argument a verb''s translation does not send. Proven against a real connector, including a delete scoped to another tenant leaving the row untouched. Adversarial review fixes refuse a key that would displace the predicate, make the startup check verb-aware, refuse a payload on a delete, and pin that a key never falls back to the body. Also moves rustls to 0.23.45 for RUSTSEC-2026-0285.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq3blCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd7IQADM28CGYl56xQtHJ8l2GiMtG\n1bi8wuHsCP12n2yCdAY